{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a nickel-catalyzed transamidation of secondary aliphatic amides. The strategy involves activating the secondary amide via N-Boc functionalization to weaken the C-N bond, followed by nickel-catalyzed coupling with various amine nucleophiles to yield new secondary or tertiary amides. This method overcomes the high kinetic and thermodynamic barriers typically associated with aliphatic amide transamidation.",
